  "notes": "Wallet carried in hand, set on the white desk at t=4.5, then the wearer walks to the kitchen (out of shot t=8.5-19.0) and returns to the same desk, where the wallet is still lying at t=19.5-25.0. Two in-shot ranges for that reason. Repeated `carried` and `nothing_happened` markers are deliberate: a window's expected answer comes from the events inside its span, so a state that lasts across windows needs a marker in each. On the desk the wallet is 63-100 px on target at 720p -- below the ~128 px identity floor, so this clip can score grounding and events but not identity.",
